  "term": "flunitrazepam",
  "definition": "Flunitrazepam is a benzodiazepine with effects similar to diazepam that can interfere with learning by causing anterograde amnesia, meaning difficulty forming new memories after taking it. Reports also link it to drug-facilitated sexual assault and possible violent behavior.",
